  "artifact_text": "### Observations and Ruled-Out Leads\n\n* Pod logs for `orders-api-7b7dfdc66d-s2556` show repeated warnings: `database orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432 not reachable ([Errno -2] Name or service not known), retrying`.\n* The Kubernetes services in `demo-apps` expose `orders-db` on port 5432, while no service named `orders-db-primary` exists.\n* Deployment log CI-2459 recorded changing ConfigMap `orders-config` parameter `DB_HOST` to `orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432` at 12:46:07Z.\n* Pod crash or restart loops were ruled out because pod container status shows state running with zero restarts.\n* Complete database outage was ruled out because `orders-db` remains active and older pod replica `orders-api-85f8f9f4f-j8vhm` logs normal serving.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nConfigMap `orders-config` configured `DB_HOST` with nonexistent hostname `orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432` before the primary database service was provisioned, failing readiness probes with HTTP 503.\n\n### Recommended Action\n\nThe orders team must revert `DB_HOST` in ConfigMap `orders-config` back to `orders-db.demo-apps.svc:5432` until the database team creates the primary service.",
